# Staff recovery hotkey. Fires regardless of which app has focus (unless the
# app has established a blocking active keyboard grab — verified on real
# hardware in Phase 2 that GCompris-qt and TuxMath, the worst case, do not).
#
# Ctrl+Alt+Shift+Escape, not an F-key: chosen in Phase 6 over the F12 combo
# used for the Phase 2 gate testing because F12 requires the Fn key on a lot
# of laptop keyboards, which is exactly the kind of thing that trips up
# non-technical teaching staff in an actual emergency.
"/opt/classpad/scripts/recovery.sh"
    control+alt+shift + Escape
